our webserver configuration or contact your web host.','','8.1.7'),(7474,'The GD Library for PHP is enabled, but was compiled without support for functions used by the rotate and desaturate effects. It was probably compiled using the official GD libraries from http://www.libgd.org instead of the GD library bundled with PHP. You should recompile PHP --with-gd using the bundled GD library. See <a href=\"http://php.net/manual/book.image.php\">the PHP manual</a>.','','none'),(7475,'Available Vocabularies','','8.1.7'),(7476,'Name (autocomplete)','','none'),(7477,'When printing URL paths, how to transform the case of the filter value. Do not use this unless with Postgres as it uses case sensitive comparisons.','','none'),(7478,'Specify which display or custom URL this display will link to.','','8.1.7'),(7479,'This will add a more link to the bottom of this view, which will link to the page view. If you have more than one page view, the link will point to the display specified in \'Link display\' section under pager. You can override the URL at the link display setting.','','none'),(7480,'When printing URL paths, how to transform the case of the filter value.','','8.1.7'),(7481,'This will appear in the URL after the ? to identify this filter. Cannot be blank. Only letters, digits and the dot (\".\"), hyphen (\"-\"), underscore (\"_\"), and tilde (\"~\") characters are allowed.','','none'),(7482,'This identifier has illegal characters.','','none'),(7483,'The field that is going to be used as the OPML URL attribute for each row.','','none'),(7484,'[user:display-name],\n\nYour account on [site:name] has been blocked.\n\n--  [site:name] team','','8.1.9'),(7485,'Bundle assigned to the auto-created entities.','','none'),(7486,'Add a new @entity_type.','','none'),(7487,'Unpublish comment','','8.1.9'),(7488,'Teaser','','8.1.9'),(7489,'Cancel the selected user account(s)','','8.1.9'),(7490,'Items per page','','8.1.7'),(7491,'<p>Choose a language from the list, or choose \"Custom language...\" at the end of the list.</p><p>Click the \"Add language\" button when you are done choosing your language.</p><p>When adding a custom language, you will get an additional form where you can provide the name, code, and direction of the language.</p>','','8.1.9'),(7492,'<p>The language name is used throughout the site for all users and is written in English. Names of built-in languages can be translated using the Interface Translation module, and names of both built-in and custom languages can be translated using the Configuration Translation module.</p>','','8.1.9'),(7493,'<p>Choose if the language is a \"Left to right\" or \"Right to left\" language.</p><p>Note that not all themes support \"Right to left\" layouts, so test your theme if you are using \"Right to left\".</p>','','8.1.9'),(7494,'<p>To reorder the languages on your site, use the drag icons next to each language.</p><p>The order shown here is the display order for language lists on the site such as in the language switcher blocks provided by the Interface Translation and Content Translation modules.</p><p>When you are done with reordering the languages, click the \"Save configuration\" button for the changes to take effect.</p>','','8.1.9'),(7495,'<p>You can change the default language of the site by choosing one of your configured languages as default. The site will use the default language in situations where no choice is made but a language should be set, for example as the language of the displayed interface.</p>','','8.1.9'),(7496,'<p>Operations are provided for editing and deleting your languages.</p><p>You can edit the name and the direction of the language.</p><p>Deleted languages can be added back at a later time. Deleting a language will remove all interface translations associated with it, and content in this language will be set to be language neutral. Note that you cannot delete the default language of the site.</p>','','8.1.9'),(7497,'View or edit the configuration.','','8.1.9'),